module undeclared_assign_fail

//@ expect-fail: not declared

// Reassignment with `=` requires the variable to already exist. `x, y = 7`
// used to silently invent x and y as locals (and broadcast 7 into both) —
// that was a type-checker bug, not a feature. Now it is a hard error; use
// `:=` to declare. (Single `x = 7` on an undeclared name is the same bug
// without the comma; multi-return `x, y = f()` likewise.)
main :: fun() {
	x, y = 7
	print(x, y)
}
